{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZwXAxuVLok99Pmtw7ZZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, here's what I found:\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Errors use sealed class `ApiException` hierarchy (`ResourceNotFoundException` → 404, `ConflictException` → 409)\n- All error responses follow the `ApiError` envelope with `code`, `message`, `fields`\n- Controllers inject repositories and throw exceptions for errors\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions\n- In-memory repositories use `ConcurrentHashMap` for thread safety\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` - add `status` field (enum `OrderStatus`)\n2. `OrderController.kt` - add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint\n3. `OrderRepository.kt` - add method to find shipments by orderId\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - add method to find shipments by orderId\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` - reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n6. `ApiError.kt` - may need new error codes (checking current ones first)\n7. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - add tests for cancel endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n- Atomicity of cancel operation (must be all-or-nothing if CONFIRMED shipment exists)\n- Thread safety of concurrent updates\n- Backwards compatibility (new orders must default to ACTIVE)\n\n**Open questions:** None blocking - the ticket is clear about all cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE`, `CANCELLED`. Add `status: OrderStatus` field to `Order` class. Ensure new orders in `OrderController.create()` initialize with `ACTIVE`.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: \n   - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` method\n   - Inject `InMemoryShipmentRepository`\n   - Implementation: check order exists (404 if not), check no CONFIRMED shipments (409 if any), if already CANCELLED return unchanged, otherwise set to CANCELLED and cancel all CREATED shipments\n   \n3. **OrderRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId()` method to ShipmentRepository (or add to OrderRepository's responsibilities).\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to retrieve all shipments for an order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: In `create()` method, check if the order exists and is not CANCELLED; if CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException` with 409.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt**: May need to add new error codes like `ORDER_CANCELLED` or `SHIPMENT_NOT_ALLOWED_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER` - but will review existing codes first.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests:\n   - Cancel an active order returns 200 with cancelled status\n   - Cancel a cancelled order succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and order stays ACTIVE\n   - Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n   - After cancel, creating shipment for that order fails with 409\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: May need test for creating shipment on cancelled order.\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Adding a `CancelOrderService` class: rejected because the logic is simple enough to live in the controller, and the repository is in-memory so no complex transaction handling is needed.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Check | Write | Response |\n|------|------|-------|-------|----------|\n| Order not found | Order by ID | - | - | 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND |\n| CONFIRMED shipment exists | Order, all shipments | hasConfirmed | - | 409 CONFLICT |\n| Already CANCELLED | Order, all shipments | already CANCELLED | - | 200 (same order) |\n| ACTIVE with CREATED shipments | Order, all shipments | - | Order→CANCELLED, Shipments→CANCELLED | 200 (cancelled order) |\n| Retry cancelled order | Order, all shipments | already CANCELLED | - | 200 (same order) |\n| Create shipment for CANCELLED | Order, Shipment | order.status==CANCELLED | - | 409 CONFLICT |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Happy path - cancel active order with created shipments → status 200, order CANCELLED, shipments CANCELLED\n- Test 2: Idempotency - cancel already cancelled order → status 200, no changes\n- Test 3: Conflict - cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment → status 409, nothing changes\n- Test 4: Not found - cancel non-existent order → status 404\n- Test 5: Shipment creation on cancelled order → status 409\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1185,"cache_read_input_tokens":24321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1185},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36a63886-9390-40fc-84ed-9e957757fb30","uuid":"089e6232-78cf-4f57-8156-d9d66fd240fd","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:29:37.052Z","request_id":"req_011CfZwXAc5PQHDcbgkjdRud"}
